Z||000000||overlord||04-19-99||12:17 PM||||hallo, my 84 fiero has the 2.5 4 and i was wondering what kind of engine would be the best for performacne (im not rich either.).<br>The previous owner didnt tune up this car on a regular basis. I bought it, drove it home 300 k, and thought it was a little sllugish. turned out it had been running on 3 cylinders for the last 3 years, and man, u should of seen the ingnintion wires, sparking left and right.  But thats all fixed up now but the poor little 4 cylinder just insnt 100% anymore.  If someone could point me in the direction of the best engine swap for a 84 fiero s.e. Even better, (i dont know jack about enignes), what kind of car would have a good v6 engine for my fiero...thanx
Z||000001||PaUL||04-19-99||06:13 PM||||engines that have the same bolt pattern are:<br>1) GM 2.8 V6<br>2) Gm 3.1 V6<br>3) GM 3.4 v6<br>4) GM 3.4 twin cam 24valve V6<br>5) GM 3.8 v6 with or without supercharger<br>6) Isuzu 4 cycl with or without turbo<br>7) GM 1.8 4 cycl with or without turbo (made in Brazil)<br>
Z||000002||PaUL||04-19-99||06:17 PM||||oh yes forgot one<br>9) GM quad 4
Z||000003||Carrolles||04-23-99||11:17 AM||||The 3.4 from a 93 through 95 camaro/firebird is a good match.  These motors are in the 200+ hp range and bolt up to the trans ok.  You will have to move the starter to the opposite side of the engine which requires drilling a mounting hole in an angled boss on the block.  Not hard to do if you have access to the proper drilling jig.  Ed. Parks at the Fiero Factory in Alabama has the tooling to do this.  He can be reached at    Fierofactory@juno.com.
